  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add approximately 5 at.% Al to an elemental Cr coating by co-sputtering.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5 at.% Al will produce finely dispersed Al-rich precipitates in the Cr coating.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al will segregate during deposition and initial oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation of Al-rich regions will form Al2O3.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Al2O3 will form a continuous barrier at coating grain boundaries and/or the Cr/Zr interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 barrier will inhibit Cr–Zr interdiffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified coating will retain a protective chromia surface scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to elemental Cr, the Al-modified coating will show reduced or delayed Cr–Zr interdiffusion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to elemental Cr, the Al-modified coating will have improved coating integrity.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to elemental Cr, the Al-modified coating will have enhanced oxidation resistance in both PWR primary water and high-temperature steam.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elemental Cr coatings on zirconium-alloy cladding can peel and crack during high-temperature steam oxidation.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Premature failure of the elemental Cr baseline in high-temperature steam is caused by accelerated Cr–Zr interdiffusion.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Cr–5 at.% Al coating is applicable in PWR primary water at approximately 320 °C for exposures of 20–60 days.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Cr–5 at.% Al coating is applicable to transient steam exposure at temperatures up to approximately 1200 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The continuity and uniformity of the Al2O3 barrier depend on deposition and subsequent oxidation conditions.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al2O3 provides significant resistance to high-temperature oxidation and corrosion and is more stable than chromium oxide under some aggressive conditions.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
